0:{"rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[["$","$L2",null,{"study":{"id":"solarwinds","title":"The update everyone trusted","category":"Supply-chain incident","year":"2020","subtitle":"The SolarWinds Orion compromise","fictional":false,"difficulty":"Threat intelligence","summary":"A trusted software-update path became a route for compromise, showing why supply-chain evidence and follow-on activity must be analyzed separately.","story":["Organizations discovered that affected SolarWinds Orion builds could distribute malicious code through a trusted update mechanism. The incident raised immediate questions about which versions were present, which systems communicated with attacker infrastructure, and what subsequent access occurred.","CISA issued emergency mitigation guidance. The response required more than removing one file: investigators needed to consider identity, trust, cloud access, persistence, and the integrity of management systems.","The case demonstrates the value of build records, update provenance, authentication logs, endpoint telemetry, and provider cooperation. Presence of an affected product does not prove the same follow-on impact in every organization. Technical compromise, operational intrusion, and public attribution are different analytical layers."],"timeline":[{"date":"2020","event":"Compromise and investigation become public."},{"date":"December 2020","event":"CISA issues Emergency Directive 21-01."},{"date":"2021 onward","event":"Technical analysis, response guidance, and attribution discussions continue."}],"issue":"How to investigate and respond to compromise delivered through trusted software and management relationships.","holding":"Defensive lesson: establish product exposure, investigate follow-on activity, protect identity and management trust, and avoid assuming uniform impact across victims.","lessons":["Inventory software and management dependencies.","Preserve build, deployment, and identity records.","Distinguish exposure from confirmed follow-on access.","Use coordinated containment and trusted recovery.","Keep attribution confidence separate from observed technique."],"questions":["Which records connect an update to later account activity?","Why is removing the affected version alone insufficient?","What would you include in a supply-chain intelligence requirement?"],"sources":["solarwinds","mitre","nist-ir"],"topics":["5.1","5.3","5.6"]}}],[["$","script","script-0",{"src":"/_next/static/chunks/07qngb6s2_y2q.js","async":true}]],["$","$L3",null,{"children":["$","$4",null,{"name":"Next.MetadataOutlet","children":"$@5"}]}]]}],"isPartial":false,"staleTime":300,"varyParams":null,"buildId":"mMiCr23A_-Cpk0hZkfT7X"}
